Team,

June summary across the three units:

Unit 100: P-101B abnormal bearing noise under watch (WO-2270). K-301
vibration trend approaching alert - spectrum analysis booked (see
Suresh's note). E-204 bundle cleaning confirmed for August.

Unit 200: PSV-210 suspected passing, bench test in progress (WO-3070).
C-220 DP trend under process engineering review (WO-3058). P-201A
running well after the May bearing change (WO-3064, INS-605).

Unit 300: quiet month. P-301 thermal scan added to routes after the
March overheating (WO-4033). T-301 roof drain function test passed
(INS-704).

Top recurring theme this quarter remains sealing systems - the P-101A
history (three seal failures, suction design review now in the August
scope) and P-201A packing. Proposal for a plant-wide sealing survey goes
to the reliability meeting on Tuesday.

Vikram
